     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Anu folded a sheet of paper twice and the creases made a right angle.\n\"They are perpendicular,\" said her teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "perpendicular",
     "parallel",
     "set square"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Two lines are perpendicular if they meet at a right angle of 90 degrees. A paper fold can make a perpendicular: fold a line onto itself.\nParallel lines never meet and stay the same distance apart. We can draw them with a set square and ruler by sliding one set square along another.\nFolding paper in the same way twice gives parallel creases."
    }
